### Geometry: the setup of DetectorConstruction.cc (from the top: lead layer,
### steel plate, top TOF, middle TOF, Si/YSO stack, bottom TOF) plus an
### ILLUSTRATIVE target and the paper's Compton camera in place of the stack.
### Positions are placeholders to show the commands. Free space between the
### Al2 plate under the middle TOF (z = -32.5 cm) and the top of the stack is
### z = -38.4 to -32.5 cm; with the stack off it reaches the Al3 plate (-52.2 cm).
### The lead layer on top (/tof/det/absorber) is the degrader; /tof/degrader/...
### can add another slab.

# Target (未知材料): 20 x 20 x 2 cm Fe at z = -36.5 to -34.5 cm
/tof/target/enable true
/tof/target/material G4_Fe
/tof/target/size 20 20 2 cm
/tof/target/position 0 0 -35.5 cm

# The paper's camera instead of the Si/YSO stack, looking up:
# CH2 at z = -40 cm, CH1 at -42.5 cm, CH0 at -46 cm
/tof/det/stack false
/tof/det/camera true
/tof/camera/position 0 0 -40 cm
/tof/camera/rotateX 0 deg

# Extra passive boxes: name material x y z dx dy dz unit (centre, full sizes), e.g.
#/tof/blocks/add PbFloor G4_Pb 0 0 -75 80 80 5 cm
/tof/blocks/clear

/update
